  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the given reactions</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Sn</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Sn</mi></math>&nbsp;the electrode potentials are ; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Sn</mi></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Sn</mi></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>010</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The magnitude of standard electrode potential for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup></math> is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>(Nearest integer)</p>",
